.Dd August 28, 2026
.Dt BRFS 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm brfs
.Nd BrFS kernel event tap (VOP_INOTIFY interposition + change-event ring)
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Cd "kldload brfs"
.Pp
In
.Pa loader.conf :
.Cd brfs_load="YES"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
kernel module is the only change feed of the BrFS replication system.
It interposes the
.Fn vop_inotify
slot of the vnode operation vectors of watched filesystems (UFS and ZFS
alike, at the VOP dispatch layer), keeps the
.Dv VIRF_INOTIFY / VIRF_INOTIFY_PARENT
gate flags set on vnodes under registered watch roots, and delivers
fixed-size 512-byte event records
.Pq Vt struct brfs_event
through a fixed-size ring behind the
.Pa /dev/brfs
character device.
.Pp
Events carry an operation
(create, modify, delete, move_from, move_to, attrib, overflow),
a rename cookie pairing move_from with move_to, filesystem id, directory
and subject fileids, the subject generation number, and the last path
component.
No path resolution happens in the kernel.
When the ring wraps, in-band
.Dv BRFS_OP_OVERFLOW
markers are injected; the daemon treats them as a rescan trigger.
.Pp
The tap is emit-all: it performs no lineage filtering.
Consumers discard events whose directory fileids are outside their
registered roots.
The interposition is a runtime assertion on
.Fn vop_stdinotify :
a vector whose slot has been overridden by another agent is left
untouched, and
.Nm
must remain the only interposer of
.Fn vop_inotify
(see
.Pa docs/design-decisions.md ,
gap #14).
.Ss Device
.Pa /dev/brfs
is created mode 0600, owned by root:wheel, and guarded single-open
(second
.Xr open 2
fails
.Er EBUSY ) .
It is read with ordinary
.Xr read 2
or polled via
.Xr kqueue 2
.Dv EVFILT_READ .
The following
.Xr ioctl 2
requests are defined in
.In kmod/brfs.h :
.Bl -tag -width "BRFSIOC_GETSTATS"
.It Dv BRFSIOC_ADDROOT
Register a watch root (path + op mask; mask is reserved and currently
unused, pass 0).
Idempotent; re-registering re-resolves, re-flags, and re-patches.
.It Dv BRFSIOC_DELROOT
Remove a watch root and strip the gate flags under it.
.It Dv BRFSIOC_GETSTATS
Return ring counters
.Pq Vt struct brfs_stats .
.It Dv BRFSIOC_FLUSH
Drain the ring without reading.
.El
.Ss Jails
Jails cannot load kernel modules;
.Nm
loads on the host kernel and a jailed
.Xr brfsd 8
consumes
.Pa /dev/brfs
through the jail's devfs ruleset (see
.Pa etc/devfs.rules.sample ) .
Registration is namespace-clean: a jail can only watch subtrees it can
itself resolve.
.Sh SYSCTL VARIABLES
The following variables are available under
.Va security.brfs :
.Bl -tag -width "files_flagged"
.It Va enabled
Master gate for event emission (readable and writable).
.It Va ring_size
Ring capacity in events (read-only tunable, default 4096).
.It Va log_events
Log every emitted event to the kernel message buffer (debugging).
.It Va event_count
Total events pushed since load.
.It Va ring_drops
Events dropped on ring overflow.
.It Va tap_seen
vop_inotify interposer invocations.
.It Va tap_emitted
Mutation events emitted by the tap.
.It Va dirs_flagged
Directories flagged VIRF_INOTIFY.
.It Va files_flagged
Files flagged VIRF_INOTIFY_PARENT.
.It Va test_event
Write-only: push N synthetic events (delivery-path validation).
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr brfs.conf 5 ,
.Xr brfsctl 8 ,
.Xr brfsd 8
